00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:34.120
But if you drag my mother's name through the dirt, so help me, I will.

00:23:34.380 --> 00:23:35.780
You'll have to kill me first.

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:39.570
Oh, maybe that'll be the best part.

00:24:00.220 --> 00:24:00.660
Good day.

00:24:02.070 --> 00:24:02.870
It was self-defense.

00:24:03.260 --> 00:24:04.480
Not the way I saw it.

00:24:05.180 --> 00:24:06.040
What happened?

00:24:06.520 --> 00:24:09.620
You just got through doing me the greatest favor of my life.

00:24:10.520 --> 00:24:15.080
Because now I can tell my story under oath in a courtroom where everybody can hear.

00:24:15.740 --> 00:24:17.680
The whole story about your mother.

00:24:18.360 --> 00:24:19.440
You just give me the chance!

00:24:19.960 --> 00:24:20.440
That's right.

00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:22.240
It'll be about her, not about you.

00:24:25.080 --> 00:24:26.160
But you're not gonna get that chance.

00:24:34.790 --> 00:24:35.070
Thank you.

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:37.370
This.

00:24:51.750 --> 00:24:52.410
I'm afraid so then.

00:24:53.060 --> 00:24:53.880
We're looking for a little gel.

00:24:54.180 --> 00:24:54.580
Little joke.

00:24:54.950 --> 00:24:55.870
You ain't gonna like this.

00:24:56.460 --> 00:24:57.780
He shot a fellow in Virginia City.

00:24:58.250 --> 00:24:58.550
Killed him.

00:25:00.310 --> 00:25:00.830
Oh, shit.

00:25:01.460 --> 00:25:02.540
No question about it, Ben.

00:25:03.260 --> 00:25:03.700
Where is he?

00:25:04.150 --> 00:25:05.590
Who was it he was supposed to have shot?

00:25:05.980 --> 00:25:07.180
One of them fellows from New Orleans.

00:25:07.580 --> 00:25:08.260
Name a cold.

00:25:10.680 --> 00:25:12.340
This Inspector LaDuke, he witnessed it.

00:25:12.920 --> 00:25:15.000
He said, little Joe just up and did it in cold blood.

00:25:15.580 --> 00:25:17.940
Oh, Sheriff Brady, you know Little Joe better than that.

00:25:18.080 --> 00:25:19.860
All I know is he shot a man and run away.

00:25:20.340 --> 00:25:21.140
And we've got to find them.

00:25:21.590 --> 00:25:21.830
Sure.

00:25:23.900 --> 00:25:24.140
I know.

00:25:24.890 --> 00:25:25.730
Joe will be coming home.

00:25:27.260 --> 00:25:27.640
Let us.

00:25:27.860 --> 00:25:28.860
Bring him into town to you.

00:25:30.410 --> 00:25:31.010
All right, then.

00:25:31.560 --> 00:25:32.660
Your word's good enough for me.

00:25:33.480 --> 00:25:33.740
Come on.

00:26:02.710 --> 00:26:03.270
Thank you.

00:26:08.570 --> 00:26:09.010
I was hoping.

00:26:16.220 --> 00:26:16.900
I thought you'd come.

00:26:18.490 --> 00:26:19.210
I wanted to say goodbye.

00:26:20.220 --> 00:26:21.360
Son, you're not going anywhere.

00:26:25.370 --> 00:26:26.130
There's always a choice.

00:26:27.700 --> 00:26:29.680
Here it's the choice between running away or...

00:26:30.220 --> 00:26:31.120
Facing up to what's happened.

00:26:33.580 --> 00:26:34.540
What did happen in town?

00:26:36.230 --> 00:26:37.170
And I went to see Le Duc.

00:26:37.860 --> 00:26:38.920
in spite of what you promised.

00:26:40.730 --> 00:26:41.590
I promised I wouldn't harm him.

00:26:41.610 --> 00:26:42.530
I didn't say I wouldn't see him.

00:26:44.460 --> 00:26:45.900
While I was talking to him, Cole came in.

00:26:46.760 --> 00:26:47.600
Are you going to do a fight?

00:26:48.650 --> 00:26:49.750
Peter was gone and I killed him.

00:26:58.890 --> 00:26:59.370
is the

00:27:01.050 --> 00:27:02.830
Sheriff's wondering why you ran away.

00:27:04.920 --> 00:27:07.060
a lot of choice with Inspector LeDuc, the only witness.

00:27:07.420 --> 00:27:08.980
Your word against his.

00:27:09.820 --> 00:27:11.400
People of Virginia City know you and I.

00:27:12.120 --> 00:27:12.940
I know they trust you.

00:27:14.230 --> 00:27:14.990
Oh, that's not the...

00:27:15.060 --> 00:27:15.220
Right.

00:27:15.610 --> 00:27:16.450
What is the problem?

00:27:19.600 --> 00:27:21.020
LeDuc told me what he'd do at the trial.

00:27:22.870 --> 00:27:24.070
He said he'd get up in front of that home.

00:27:24.120 --> 00:27:24.420
town.

00:27:25.590 --> 00:27:26.710
Tell all those dirty lies

00:27:29.240 --> 00:27:29.680
without my mother.

00:27:30.250 --> 00:27:35.840
You were running away to protect your mother's name, is that it?

00:27:37.660 --> 00:27:38.200
Yes, that's it.

00:27:45.680 --> 00:27:47.840
Your mother begged me to stand trial in New Orleans,

00:27:48.720 --> 00:27:50.280
no matter what the consequences to her.

00:27:58.340 --> 00:27:58.980
Stay, Joe.

00:28:00.090 --> 00:28:04.970
I can't let you make the same mistake. You come home with me now.

00:28:06.470 --> 00:28:08.460
All morning, we'll ride into town together.

00:28:15.260 --> 00:28:23.500
Son, you've always trusted me in a way in your life.

00:28:31.630 --> 00:28:37.720
Come on, guys.

00:29:10.840 --> 00:29:11.540
Brought to you, prisoner.

00:29:11.760 --> 00:29:13.690
Thanks, Ben. What have you got to say?

00:29:14.990 --> 00:29:15.970
Shot him in self-defense.

00:29:16.520 --> 00:29:17.700
Cole's gun was in his holster.

00:29:18.990 --> 00:29:20.270
It's impossible, he drew first.

00:29:20.410 --> 00:29:22.340
It was there. Why'd you run away?

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:25.340
Maybe I figured he'd be framed, like what's happening now.

00:29:25.520 --> 00:29:26.700
You know better than that, Adam.

00:29:27.060 --> 00:29:28.020
You'll get a fair trial.

00:29:29.110 --> 00:29:29.830
Gotta lock you up, son.

00:29:38.530 --> 00:29:39.370
I'll be back in a few minutes.

00:30:02.080 --> 00:30:04.280
I saw you riding into town with your son.

00:30:04.400 --> 00:30:06.760
If you come to plead for him, you're wasting your time.

00:30:09.010 --> 00:30:16.140
The Duke, you didn't come to Virginia City for my son. You came for me.

00:30:16.880 --> 00:30:19.400
I do rather admire you for bringing him in.

00:30:19.520 --> 00:30:21.300
Shows a certain respect for the law.

00:30:21.640 --> 00:30:22.040
Respect?

00:30:24.240 --> 00:30:26.020
My son tells me you saw the shooting.

00:30:27.950 --> 00:30:29.570
He also tells me you can clear him.

00:30:31.570 --> 00:30:33.310
Every criminal claims he's innocent.

00:30:34.400 --> 00:30:38.300
Don't call my son a criminal, and let's stop beating around the bush.

00:30:38.750 --> 00:30:41.290
You came to Virginia City to close the LaRouche murder case,

00:30:41.350 --> 00:30:42.950
well, I'm gonna give you a chance to do just that.

00:30:43.220 --> 00:30:44.520
Are you offering me a deal?

00:30:45.270 --> 00:30:46.670
I'm offering you a deal.

00:30:49.430 --> 00:30:54.350
You clear my board to New Orleans with ya.

00:31:10.940 --> 00:31:29.360
me to purge him myself. I'm officer of the law, the truth isn't open to women, but suppose I do make this compromise, would you return with me unarmed, this hand alone, just you and me, on horse.

00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:34.580
Yes, I would.

00:31:34.780 --> 00:31:39.970
And would you give me a promise, your word, that you'd make no attempt to escape?

00:31:40.390 --> 00:31:41.170
That would be my word.

00:31:43.130 --> 00:31:45.330
How long would it take you to get the horses and provisions ready?

00:31:46.650 --> 00:31:47.170
An hour?

00:31:47.820 --> 00:31:50.020
In an hour and a half, I'll have time to get outfitted.

00:31:51.210 --> 00:31:54.220
Meet you at the gym, please, son. We'll leave directly from there.

00:31:54.670 --> 00:31:58.540
And Cartwright, you should feel relieved.

00:31:59.350 --> 00:31:59.970
Every crim...

00:32:00.060 --> 00:32:02.200
always is who finally surrenders himself

00:32:02.200 --> 00:32:02.900
to justice.

00:32:31.920 --> 00:32:32.300
Who's coming?

00:32:36.240 --> 00:32:40.010
Inspector LeDuc. He's agreed to tell the truth about the shooting.

00:32:41.130 --> 00:32:41.930
Tell the truth? Why?

00:32:45.170 --> 00:32:51.770
We'll be back to New Orleans. We'll be back soon.

00:32:53.750 --> 00:32:57.520
Sheriff Ben says you got something you want to tell me.

00:32:58.060 --> 00:32:59.980
It's about the... the devil.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.010
I'm my associate, Mr. Tom Cole.

00:33:02.840 --> 00:33:03.820
Step over the desk, please.

00:33:06.930 --> 00:33:15.380
Save the day, but I rather confuse the fat fuser.

00:33:16.400 --> 00:33:19.940
Well, as I recall now, Cole was drunk. He drew first.

00:33:20.490 --> 00:33:22.660
Joe Cartwright fired in self-defense.

00:33:24.600 --> 00:33:26.100
What about the gun in Cole's holster?

00:33:26.570 --> 00:33:29.390
He put it there himself before he died. Sort of a reflex.

00:33:30.350 --> 00:33:32.270
Mister, you really was confused, wasn't you?

00:33:33.910 --> 00:33:34.770
Maybe the strange client.

00:33:36.060 --> 00:33:38.380
I rarely bungle the facts like this in New Orleans.

00:33:39.980 --> 00:33:42.630
Mister, stay in New Orleans.

00:33:43.530 --> 00:33:45.490
We need you around here like we need to play.

00:33:46.430 --> 00:33:48.210
You belong in that cell instead of Little Joe.

00:33:49.220 --> 00:33:52.180
Sure, if everybody makes mistakes, ask Ben Cartwright.

00:33:52.340 --> 00:33:54.560
All I want to ask Ben is really accept my apologies.

00:34:00.600 --> 00:34:01.020
Thank you, sir.

00:34:03.940 --> 00:34:06.200
Don't let Little Joe out of his cell until I...

00:34:06.990 --> 00:34:08.840
Well, why not? Where are you going?

00:34:11.270 --> 00:34:11.710
Let's see what happens.

00:34:26.930 --> 00:34:28.510
Little Joe will be out pretty soon, Paul.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:34.740
Oh, I know you told us not to, but how come me and Adam can't ride out about 10 miles and intercept you?

00:34:35.680 --> 00:34:38.060
A couple of eyeballs rode up on you, it wouldn't be your fault, would it?

00:34:39.790 --> 00:34:40.150
Forget it.

00:34:40.800 --> 00:34:41.940
Well, at least we can ride along with you.

00:34:42.060 --> 00:34:42.820
He can't object to that.

00:34:43.410 --> 00:34:44.290
Oh, he does object.

00:34:45.490 --> 00:34:46.490
I said I'd go alone.

00:34:47.750 --> 00:34:48.710
Now, why is that so important?

00:34:49.240 --> 00:34:49.820
What's his motive?

00:34:51.060 --> 00:34:53.960
I'm going to get my wood.

00:35:03.130 --> 00:35:03.310
Hello

00:36:05.850 --> 00:36:06.730
You're not a bad cook.

00:36:10.620 --> 00:36:14.490
Now it reminds me something happened recently.

00:36:14.690 --> 00:36:18.900
There was a case where a condemned man wanted to cook his own last meal.

00:36:19.730 --> 00:36:21.030
And then he didn't have time to eat it.

00:36:22.490 --> 00:36:23.010
So I did.

00:36:23.710 --> 00:36:24.590
You know, it was very good.

00:36:26.520 --> 00:36:27.140
Sure it was.

00:36:30.570 --> 00:36:36.180
LeDuc, why did you wait 20 years to come after me?

00:36:36.450 --> 00:36:39.860
I'm an officer of the law. I'm subject to the orders of my superiors.

00:36:41.280 --> 00:36:48.030
I just can't believe that your superiors suddenly decided after 20 years that I should be brought back.

00:36:48.480 --> 00:36:50.040
Well, I made that decision myself.

00:36:50.600 --> 00:36:53.060
Of course, I had to become an inspector before I could do so.

00:36:53.770 --> 00:36:56.390
The fact that it took 20 years is your fault, not mine.

00:36:58.240 --> 00:36:58.880
My fault?

00:36:59.810 --> 00:36:59.970
Yeah.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:07.110
Yes, I've already told you. A man with a physical handicap doesn't rise fast in police work.

00:37:09.200 --> 00:37:11.960
I told you before I don't hold myself responsible for that act.

00:37:13.750 --> 00:37:24.140
When you became a police officer, you must have figured that you'd have to take certain risks.

00:37:24.760 --> 00:37:28.420
Well, strangely enough, I used to use those same arguments with myself.

00:37:29.840 --> 00:37:29.980
I knew-

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:33.460
I knew that my hatred of you might become an obsession. I wanted to control it.

00:37:33.760 --> 00:37:34.900
I wish you'd been successful.

00:37:36.810 --> 00:37:42.470
All this for a while, but then as I watched inferior men being promoted over my head,

00:37:42.570 --> 00:37:46.550
I began to wonder whether it wasn't too charitable thoughts about you.

00:37:47.180 --> 00:37:50.870
Is that when you started to think about vengeance instead of justice?

00:37:51.210 --> 00:37:54.010
Well, didn't I have it coming to me after all the misery you've caused me?

00:37:54.130 --> 00:37:59.960
I don't believe that any man is justified in using a badge to satisfy his personal hatred.

00:38:00.120 --> 00:38:04.420
You're so cold-blooded in your thinking, Cartwright.

00:38:05.740 --> 00:38:15.990
No. I've hated men in my time, but I've been able to control myself and not allow that hatred to influence my life.

00:38:16.340 --> 00:38:23.830
Oh, why not? You're a rich man. You have sons. You've loved women and been loved by them.

00:38:26.460 --> 00:38:29.980
That smashed me of yours. It's truly been of help to you.

00:38:31.980 --> 00:38:32.560
What do you mean?

00:38:33.120 --> 00:38:38.200
The way you use it to lean on like a crutch to explain away your personal little failures

00:38:38.200 --> 00:38:41.040
and your police work with women and your relations with other people.

00:38:41.220 --> 00:38:41.860
Stop it!

00:38:42.050 --> 00:38:42.930
Well, face it!

00:38:43.590 --> 00:38:44.530
It's not your needs!

00:38:44.730 --> 00:38:47.140
You top it or I'll shoot you down!

00:38:56.910 --> 00:38:59.830
Never intended to take me all the way back to New Orleans.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:09.170
you got it all figured out haven't you how was it to happen i was to be killed while trying to

00:39:09.170 --> 00:39:13.780
escape is that it you'd like me to say yes wouldn't you so you'd be free to break your

00:39:13.780 --> 00:39:29.750
word no i don't intend to break my word i'll intend to try to escape because i'm going to get

00:39:30.030 --> 00:39:31.270
All the way to New York.

00:39:34.140 --> 00:39:37.140
Just in case you have any idea of killing me for-

00:39:37.140 --> 00:39:37.320
No!

00:39:37.620 --> 00:39:56.230
Don't wanna kill you tonight.

00:39:58.960 --> 00:39:59.980
I'm not gonna sleep tonight.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:00.980
I've been caught right.

00:40:03.510 --> 00:40:06.210
I'm not going to sleep any night while you're alive.

00:40:22.420 --> 00:40:22.720
Let's go.

00:40:23.060 --> 00:40:23.900
Warm one today.

00:40:24.440 --> 00:40:25.380
What are you waiting for?

00:40:25.480 --> 00:40:25.880
Mind up.

00:40:43.720 --> 00:40:44.440
Get away from me!

00:40:46.500 --> 00:40:47.580
Get away from me, Cartwright!

00:40:56.650 --> 00:40:58.250
I'll put a bullet through your leg.

00:40:59.240 --> 00:40:59.980
So you'll know how.

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:00.720
Todd Shields.

00:41:22.230 --> 00:41:22.790
Do you have another gun?

00:41:23.580 --> 00:41:24.280
This will do it.

00:41:44.460 --> 00:41:44.560
you know.

00:41:45.290 --> 00:41:45.590
What's that?

00:41:46.020 --> 00:41:46.220
Well,

00:41:49.670 --> 00:41:50.470
They won't have to say.

00:41:50.630 --> 00:41:51.130
Calps.

00:41:51.430 --> 00:41:52.190
They're up to horses.

00:42:03.930 --> 00:42:04.950
as far as the nearest settlement.

00:42:09.720 --> 00:42:10.960
That's a way station up ahead.

00:42:11.960 --> 00:42:12.500
How far?

00:42:14.580 --> 00:42:15.120
20 miles.

00:42:16.860 --> 00:42:17.220
miles.

00:42:19.220 --> 00:42:20.060
Over those hills.

00:42:22.850 --> 00:42:23.490
I don't know what it says.

00:42:25.660 --> 00:42:26.300
without water.

00:43:38.760 --> 00:43:39.340
Rest of class.

00:43:40.810 --> 00:43:41.510
Got to keep moving.

00:43:42.570 --> 00:43:43.430
This son will kill you.

00:43:44.550 --> 00:43:45.010
I can't.

00:43:45.220 --> 00:43:45.500
anymore

00:43:47.590 --> 00:43:48.370
Gotta get to work.

00:44:23.930 --> 00:44:27.550
Stay away.

00:44:29.210 --> 00:44:29.930
I don't need your help.

00:44:32.040 --> 00:44:32.660
Let me help you.

00:44:33.390 --> 00:44:34.290
I said stay awake.

00:44:39.920 --> 00:44:43.020
Krieger, waiting 20 years for this.

00:45:43.850 --> 00:45:59.290
Let me give you a sec.

00:46:03.530 --> 00:46:26.290
You brought me in, why didn't you leave me out there to die?

00:46:27.360 --> 00:46:28.200
Why'd you die out there?

00:46:30.960 --> 00:46:32.060
Both men better off.

00:46:35.700 --> 00:46:37.000
When's the next stage leave for the East?

00:46:37.240 --> 00:46:38.620
Uh, it's due in some time.

00:46:40.700 --> 00:46:40.980
Keep going.

00:46:45.380 --> 00:46:46.800
It's none in New Orleans for you.

00:46:47.880 --> 00:46:49.680
You were warned for my arrest, don't you?

00:46:51.960 --> 00:46:52.620
You were right.

00:46:52.740 --> 00:46:55.280
I intended to kill you before we ever got there.

00:46:57.200 --> 00:46:59.960
But you can't kill without hatin' out of the head.

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:03.400
Hate is gone. It's out of a relief.

00:47:08.940 --> 00:47:10.080
The warrant was never any good, was it?

00:47:10.750 --> 00:47:14.760
You were cleared 20 years ago by everybody except me.

00:47:16.990 --> 00:47:19.570
That letter the judge sent you, I intercepted it.

00:47:21.540 --> 00:47:23.140
Why didn't you leave me out there?

00:47:32.430 --> 00:47:35.000
Can you, uh, rustle up some food for a couple of hungry men?

00:47:35.580 --> 00:47:38.810
You're coming here together.

00:47:39.660 --> 00:47:41.840
You too, mister. Just give me a couple of...

00:47:44.870 --> 00:47:45.490
Well, let's wash it.
